== The API change (same across all files) ==
REMOVED (must not appear anywhere in core/doc/spec except as history): zlink_send_part,
zlink_send_part_rid, zlink_request_part, zlink_reply_part, zlink_publish_part, zlink_recv_part,
zlink_router_recv_part, zlink_subscribe_part, zlink_xpub_recv_part, the type zlink_part_flag_t and
ZLINK_PART_MORE / ZLINK_PART_FINAL, and the "one record from first MORE to FINAL on the same thread"
rule + mid-sequence BUSY + failed-FINAL-discards-staged-prefix rule.
ADDED (whole-message, array + count; signatures verbatim from README): zlink_send, zlink_send_rid,
zlink_request, zlink_reply, zlink_publish, zlink_recv, zlink_router_recv, zlink_subscribe,
zlink_xpub_recv. KEPT: zlink_stream_recv_packet, zlink_multipart_close, zlink_completion_*.
Contracts D63-6..8: capacity<part_count → non-consuming ZLINK_RECV_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL(ENOBUFS)+needed
count, retry gets same record; STREAM RAW recv via zlink_recv (1 part), STREAM send count==1 (empty
part to valid RID disconnects that peer); whole-record retry (no partial). part send consumes all
input slots.

